.                 * where d_left is the dependent variable, daughters_nr is the
>  number of daughters, `controls' is the vector 
.                 * of control variables, and i.tot_kids is the total children 
> fixed effects.  
.                 * 
.                 * Interpretation of Results:  
.                 * The coefficient on daughters_nr is the primary parameter of
>  interest. A positive and statistically significant 
.                 * estimate would suggest that having more daughters is associ
> ated with stronger left-leaning political preferences. 
.                 * Statistical significance will be evaluated at the 10%, 5%, 
> and 1% levels, and z-statistics will be reported. 
.                 * Residual degrees of freedom are not applicable due to the m
> aximum likelihood estimation used in logistic 
.                 * regression. 
. 
. 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * (Please check whether the suggested code autom
> atically picks up the correct statistics for your chosen regression analysis 
> and adapt if needed)
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[daughters_nr]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[daughters_nr]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "z"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local z_value = _b[daughters_nr] / _se[daughters_nr]

.                 local p_value = 2 * (1 - normal(abs(`z_value')))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 scalar coef_d_daughter = _b[daughters_nr]

.                 local interpretation "positive coefficient is in line with hy
> pothesis"

